  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1 (12 bars), vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1917 Pace & Handy sheet music (page images and LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b9/scan/), key B flat major, cut time (durations in quarter-note beats), starting after the opening quarter rest. Simplifications (chromatic notes played as the nearest drum note): the four F sharps (chromatic passing notes in bars 1, 2, 5 and 6) are played as 5 (F); the A flat in bar 2 (the blue 7th, b7) is played as 7 (A); the E natural leading into 'I've strolled' is played as 4 (E flat). Range 3 to high 1; C and D arrangements are the same notes. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums).",
